IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- PAYMENT OF BENEFITS (regulations 55 to 59).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 586 to 607.
--
-- Payment to someone on behalf of a beneficiary who cannot manage their affairs (55); payment of a very small benefit
-- in arrears (56); a payment unpaid at death (57); the single monthly payment of a benefit also payable under the
-- Quebec Pension Plan (58); withholding a benefit until evidence is furnished (59).
-- Judgments the text hands to the Minister are BOOLEAN inputs named for them. Regulation 58(2) only says which account
-- bears and which is credited with a part of a single payment; it decides nothing for the person and is encoded as two
-- BOOLEAN rules without a seat question.

§ `Part V -- Payment of benefits (regulations 55 to 59)`

§§ `Regulation 55 -- payment on behalf of a beneficiary`

-- src:587 | 55 (1) Where the Minister is satisfied, on such information or evidence as is presented to him or as he may require, that a beneficiary, by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause, is incapable of managing his own affairs, the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on behalf of such beneficiary to any person or agency that the Minister is satisfied is authorized by or pursuant to any law of Canada or of a province to manage that beneficiary’s affairs or, where it appears to the Minister that there is no person or agency so authorized, to a person or agency approved by the Minister.
@ref Reg 55(1) (src:587)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied on the information or evidence presented or required that the beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that there is no person or agency so authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or agency is approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 55(1) — the Minister may direct that a benefit be paid on behalf of a beneficiary to a person or agency`
    `the Minister is satisfied on the information or evidence presented or required that the beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs`
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary's affairs`
    `it appears to the Minister that there is no person or agency so authorized`
    `the person or agency is approved by the Minister` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied on the information or evidence presented or required that the beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs`
        AND (    `the Minister is satisfied that the person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary's affairs`
              OR (    `it appears to the Minister that there is no person or agency so authorized`
                  AND `the person or agency is approved by the Minister`))

-- src:588 | (2) Where the Minister directs, pursuant to subsection (1), that a benefit be paid on behalf of a beneficiary to a person or agency referred to in that subsection, no such benefit shall be paid to such person or agency until the person or agency, as the case may be, has undertaken in an agreement with the Minister
-- src:589 | (a) to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary in accordance with the terms of the agreement; and
-- src:590 | (b) to furnish any information or evidence and to do anything that the Act or these Regulations require the beneficiary to furnish or do.
@ref Reg 55(2) (src:588-590)
GIVEN `the person or agency has undertaken in an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary in accordance with the terms of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or agency has undertaken in the agreement to furnish any information or evidence and to do anything that the Act or these Regulations require the beneficiary to furnish or do` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 55(2) — the benefit may be paid to the person or agency the Minister has directed`
    `the person or agency has undertaken in an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary in accordance with the terms of the agreement`
    `the person or agency has undertaken in the agreement to furnish any information or evidence and to do anything that the Act or these Regulations require the beneficiary to furnish or do` MEANS
    `the person or agency has undertaken in an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary in accordance with the terms of the agreement`
        AND `the person or agency has undertaken in the agreement to furnish any information or evidence and to do anything that the Act or these Regulations require the beneficiary to furnish or do`

-- src:591 | (3) Any person or agency to whom a benefit is paid pursuant to this section on behalf of a beneficiary shall account, in a form approved by the Minister and at such time or times as he directs, to the Minister for the benefit payments received and the disbursements made of the payments.
@ref Reg 55(3) (src:591)
GIVEN `a benefit is paid to the person or agency pursuant to this section on behalf of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 55(3) — the person or agency must account to the Minister for the benefit payments received and the disbursements made`
    `a benefit is paid to the person or agency pursuant to this section on behalf of a beneficiary` MEANS
    `a benefit is paid to the person or agency pursuant to this section on behalf of a beneficiary`

§§ `Regulation 56 -- payment of a very small benefit at intervals`

-- src:594 | 56 Where any benefit the basic monthly amount of which is less than $2 becomes payable to a person to whom no pension is then payable under the Old Age Security Act, the Minister may direct that the benefit shall be paid in arrears at intervals, not greater than yearly, specified by the Minister.
@ref Reg 56 (src:594)
GIVEN `the basic monthly amount of the benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `a pension is then payable to the person under the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 56 — the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid in arrears at intervals`
    `the basic monthly amount of the benefit`
    `a pension is then payable to the person under the Old Age Security Act` MEANS
    `the basic monthly amount of the benefit` LESS THAN 2
        AND (NOT `a pension is then payable to the person under the Old Age Security Act`)

@ref Reg 56 (src:594)
GIVEN `the interval in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 56 — an interval the Minister specifies is not greater than yearly` `the interval in months` MEANS
    `the interval in months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the interval in months` AT MOST 12

§§ `Regulation 57 -- a benefit payment unpaid at death`

-- src:597 | 57 A benefit payment may be paid to the estate of a deceased beneficiary, or if there is no estate, to a person or agency designated by the Minister, where
-- src:598 | (a) an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary; or
-- src:599 | (b) a benefit payment made to the beneficiary or made on behalf of the beneficiary by cheque or otherwise is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary’s death.
@ref Reg 57 (src:597-599)
GIVEN `an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit payment made to or on behalf of the beneficiary is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an estate of the deceased beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cr2 Payee of a benefit payment unpaid at death`
`reg 57 — the payee of a benefit payment unpaid at death`
    `an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary`
    `a benefit payment made to or on behalf of the beneficiary is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death`
    `there is an estate of the deceased beneficiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary`
                OR `a benefit payment made to or on behalf of the beneficiary is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death`)
           THEN `nobody under regulation 57`
        IF `there is an estate of the deceased beneficiary` THEN `the estate of the deceased beneficiary`
        OTHERWISE `a person or agency designated by the Minister`

§§ `Regulation 58 -- single payment of benefits`

-- src:602 | 58 (1) For the purposes of paragraph 89(1)(j) of the Act, where the Government of Canada paid a benefit in December 1974 to a person in respect of contributions made under the Act and under the Quebec Pension Plan, the Minister may direct that a single monthly payment be made by cheque or otherwise for as long as the beneficiary remains entitled to the benefit.
-- src:603 | (2) Where a single monthly payment is made in respect of a beneficiary, that portion of the payment calculated as provided in the Quebec Pension Plan shall, in accordance with paragraph 108(3)(b) of the Act, be charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account and the amount remitted by the Government of the Province of Quebec in respect of the benefit payable to that beneficiary under the Quebec Pension Plan shall, in accordance with paragraph 108(2)(b) of the Act, be credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account.
@ref Reg 58(1) (src:602)
GIVEN `the Government of Canada paid a benefit in December 1974 to the person in respect of contributions made under the Act and under the Quebec Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary remains entitled to the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(1) — the Minister may direct that a single monthly payment be made`
    `the Government of Canada paid a benefit in December 1974 to the person in respect of contributions made under the Act and under the Quebec Pension Plan`
    `the beneficiary remains entitled to the benefit` MEANS
    `the Government of Canada paid a benefit in December 1974 to the person in respect of contributions made under the Act and under the Quebec Pension Plan`
        AND `the beneficiary remains entitled to the benefit`

@ref Reg 58(2) (src:603)
GIVEN `a single monthly payment is made in respect of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion is calculated as provided in the Quebec Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(2) — the portion of the payment is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account`
    `a single monthly payment is made in respect of the beneficiary`
    `the portion is calculated as provided in the Quebec Pension Plan` MEANS
    `a single monthly payment is made in respect of the beneficiary` AND `the portion is calculated as provided in the Quebec Pension Plan`

@ref Reg 58(2) (src:603)
GIVEN `a single monthly payment is made in respect of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is remitted by the Government of the Province of Quebec in respect of the benefit payable under the Quebec Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(2) — the amount remitted by the Government of Quebec is credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account`
    `a single monthly payment is made in respect of the beneficiary`
    `the amount is remitted by the Government of the Province of Quebec in respect of the benefit payable under the Quebec Pension Plan` MEANS
    `a single monthly payment is made in respect of the beneficiary`
        AND `the amount is remitted by the Government of the Province of Quebec in respect of the benefit payable under the Quebec Pension Plan`

§§ `Regulation 59 -- withholding of benefits`

-- 59(1): "on 30 days written notice": the withholding may not begin until 30 days after the notice (fork F-59).
-- src:606 | 59 (1) Where evidence is required under the Act or these Regulations to determine the eligibility or continuing eligibility of any beneficiary to receive any amount payable as a benefit and where the Minister has requested such evidence and the beneficiary has not complied with the request or the Minister is not satisfied with the evidence furnished by that beneficiary, the Minister may, on 30 days written notice, withhold payment of the benefit until such time as the beneficiary has furnished the evidence and the Minister is satisfied as to the eligibility of that beneficiary to receive benefits.
-- src:607 | (2) Where payment of a benefit that has been withheld under subsection (1) is resumed, the benefit shall be paid for any portion of the period of withholding during which the beneficiary was entitled to receive benefits.
@ref Reg 59(1) (src:606)
GIVEN `the date the written notice is given to the beneficiary` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 59(1) — the earliest day payment of the benefit may be withheld` `the date the written notice is given to the beneficiary` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date the written notice is given to the beneficiary` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

@ref Reg 59(1) (src:606)
GIVEN `evidence is required under the Act or these Regulations to determine the eligibility or continuing eligibility of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has requested the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary has not complied with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is not satisfied with the evidence furnished by the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the written notice is given to the beneficiary` IS A DATE
      `the day from which payment is withheld` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 59(1) — the Minister may withhold payment of the benefit from a day`
    `evidence is required under the Act or these Regulations to determine the eligibility or continuing eligibility of the beneficiary`
    `the Minister has requested the evidence`
    `the beneficiary has not complied with the request`
    `the Minister is not satisfied with the evidence furnished by the beneficiary`
    `the date the written notice is given to the beneficiary`
    `the day from which payment is withheld` MEANS
    `evidence is required under the Act or these Regulations to determine the eligibility or continuing eligibility of the beneficiary`
        AND `the Minister has requested the evidence`
        AND (`the beneficiary has not complied with the request` OR `the Minister is not satisfied with the evidence furnished by the beneficiary`)
        AND `the day from which payment is withheld` AT LEAST
            (`reg 59(1) — the earliest day payment of the benefit may be withheld` `the date the written notice is given to the beneficiary`)

@ref Reg 59(1) (src:606)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has furnished the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied as to the eligibility of the beneficiary to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 59(1) — payment of the benefit may still be withheld`
    `the beneficiary has furnished the evidence`
    `the Minister is satisfied as to the eligibility of the beneficiary to receive benefits` MEANS
    NOT (`the beneficiary has furnished the evidence` AND `the Minister is satisfied as to the eligibility of the beneficiary to receive benefits`)

@ref Reg 59(2) (src:607)
GIVEN `payment of the benefit that had been withheld under subsection (1) is resumed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary was entitled to receive benefits on that day of the period of withholding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 59(2) — the benefit is paid for a day of the period of withholding`
    `payment of the benefit that had been withheld under subsection (1) is resumed`
    `the beneficiary was entitled to receive benefits on that day of the period of withholding` MEANS
    `payment of the benefit that had been withheld under subsection (1) is resumed`
        AND `the beneficiary was entitled to receive benefits on that day of the period of withholding`
